PS5 HDMI: VRR test 25, replay a captured pre-block 1:1 (hdmi.vrr_prep_raw)  [ps5-bazzite-deck]

hsgodd: with test 24 every visible stock message of the VRR switch is replicated except
the pre-block (stock id ~0x018d), whose constants were lifted from a 4K capture (0x7061,
0x7215, 0x6207, 0x621b, 0x7070) and may be wrong for other modes. hdmi.vrr_prep_raw
(runtime, hex) sends a captured pre-block 1:1 instead of ours: the whole ICC query (its
12-byte header is replaced) or only the I2C body. Logged as "VRR prep RAW" with the
chip's status, and in the ICC trace. Also: the UPDCTRL latch after the pre-block
(vrr_updctrl) now defaults to off, since stock's capture has none.
---

--- a/drivers/ps5/hdmi.c
+++ b/drivers/ps5/hdmi.c
@@ -805,7 +805,7 @@
 MODULE_PARM_DESC(vrr_phy_tail, "VRR test 19: stock PHY tail in the first PHY message (1 full, 2 minimal, 0 none)");
 static u32 phy_reply_v;
 static bool phy_reply_ok;
-static unsigned int vrr_updctrl = 0x10;
+static unsigned int vrr_updctrl;	/* test 25: 0, stock has no 0x10 latch after its pre-block (hsgodd's capture) */
